RBO Hand 2 (TU Berlin)                         [relationship: inspired-by]
  Author:    Raphael Deimel and Oliver Brock, Robotics and Biology Laboratory,
             Technische Universität Berlin
  Source:    https://depositonce.tu-berlin.de/items/8b6c48a6-dcc1-4466-8eda-cb0df6136b1b
             ("RBO Hand 2 CAD Files", DOI 10.14279/depositonce-5831)
  License:   CC-BY-SA-4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
             International), corroborated at
             https://www.naturalmachinemotioninitiative.com/rbo-hand-2
  Basis:     What this cartridge took is the PRINCIPLE that compliance can live
             in the material itself — a flexure that bends because of what it
             is made of, instead of a discrete joint with a bearing. The RBO
             Hand 2 CAD files are moulds for casting pneumatic PneuFlex
             actuators; this cartridge is a printed multi-material gripper with
             V-notch living hinges and no pneumatics. No RBO Hand 2 file was
             downloaded, opened, copied or adapted.
  Caution:   CC-BY-SA-4.0 is a COPYLEFT licence: a work that IS a derivative of
             the RBO Hand 2 CAD files must be shared alike under CC-BY-SA-4.0
